3}\\hspace{0.222em}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139544976 17592186576411 true] [17592186344968 1074 "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x+w & =w &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ x+(-x+w) & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{adding }x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (x+(-x))+w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A2}\\,\\,] \\\\ 0+w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom  A3}\\,] \\\\ w+(-w) & =x+w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{adding }-w\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ w+(-w) & =x+(w+(-w)) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom  A2}\\,] \\\\ 0 & =x+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A4}\\,\\,] \\\\ 0 & =x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom  A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139544976 17592186576411 false] [17592186344987 1071 "Consider the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$ and the vector $\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2k \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find the value of $k$ such that $\\mathbf{b}\\in \\text{Null}(A).$" 13194139544976 17592186576411 true] [17592186344987 1071 "Consider the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$ and the vector $b=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2k \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find the value of $k$ such that $b\\in \\text{Null}(A).$" 13194139544976 17592186576411 false] [17592186344987 1074 "If $\\mathbf{b}\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $A\\mathbf{b}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\mathbf{b} & =\\mathbf{0} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2k \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}4k-8 \\\\ 2k-4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4k-8 &=0 \\\\ 2k-4 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=2.$" 13194139544976 17592186576411 true] [17592186344987 1074 "If $b\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $Ab=0.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2k \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}4k-8 \\\\ 2k-4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4k-8 &=0 \\\\ 2k-4 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=2.$" 13194139544976 17592186576411 false] [17592186344988 1074 "We need to solve the equation $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -10 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 15\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 15\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 0 &=0 \\\\ 0 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is ${x}_{1}$, and we have two free variables, ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ in terms of ${x}_{2}$  and ${x}_{3}.$\n\nFrom the first equation we get ${x}_{1}=2{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3},$ so the set of all the solutions of $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\hspace{0.222em}:\\hspace{0.222em}{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in \\mathbb{R}\\right\\}.\n$$" 13194139544976 17592186576411 true] [17592186344988 1074 "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -10 